# `point.x += step * point.speed`: the sum's first operand is the read of the field, made before the product. The operands of a commutative operation stood by age, the elder first, and x86-64 reads only its
# second operand out of memory: so the read took an instruction of its own. Among the operands of a commutative operation on numbers a load stands last.
